{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780640916,"nonce":"vSnKhgyGGQabk5H8EWPcgF0JkJo=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABEd6MVA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/228","origin":"github"},"title":"Deployment: pre-class shakedown — validate the CA safety helm gate + survey/sensor carry-forwards","message":"## Purpose\n\nNext on-water deployment — **pre-class shakedown** (before the June 8 class start / dev\nfreeze), de-risking the June survey. The headline new item: the **CA safety node**\n(`ca_safety_node`) is now the **default helm gate** on BizzyBoat (replacing the nav2\nCollision Monitor), so this deployment's primary goal is to **validate it on water**.\nCarries over the unfinished #205 goals (clean survey lines, sensor/sonar readiness, OTH).\n\nMerged just before this deployment: rolker/unh_marine_navigation#64 (node),\nrolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11#43 + this repo #227 (wiring + 240 overlay).\n\n## Goal 1 — Validate the CA safety helm gate (primary)\n\nThe node replaces the Collision Monitor with a **speed-scaled, yaw-preserving slowdown +\nreverse-assisted stop** — the fix for the #205 near-miss/\"stops dead in front of the\nobstacle and can't turn off it\" deadlock. Validate:\n\n- [ ] **Pre-water gate (sim):** run the **yaw-sign-in-reverse** sim test. Until it passes,\n      `cancel_yaw_during_reverse` stays **true** (straight reverse brake) — do **not** enable\n      the yaw-passthrough path on water this deployment.\n- [ ] **Nominal survey unchanged** — no obstacle ⇒ cmd_vel passes through; speed/yaw same as before.\n- [ ] **Slowdown behaves** — boat slows earlier/proportionally to speed as an obstacle enters\n      the forward corridor, **while still able to turn** (the anti-deadlock mechanism); the\n      avoider gets room to steer clear.\n- [ ] **Reverse-assisted stop** — in the stop box the boat brakes to a stop (reverse thrust),\n      bounded by the distance/duration backstop (stern is unsensed — confirm it doesn't run\n      aft past the cap; the duration backstop is the odom-independent bound).\n- [ ] **CAMP viz** — yellow (slowdown, **sized live by speed**) + red (stop) boxes render and\n      **fill** on activation (driven by `CollisionMonitorState`); ties into #183.\n- [ ] **Sole helm publisher** — Collision Monitor is gone from the chain; the node logs a\n      warning if it ever sees \u003e1 publisher on the helm topic. Confirm no double-publish.\n- [ ] **Fallback drilled** — `use_ca_safety:=false` reverts to the Collision Monitor; confirm\n      the one-line field revert works before relying on the new gate.\n\nRelated/after: reverse-*arc* escape + rotate-in-place is the principled follow-on\n(rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11#42); recovery-BT back-off is rolker/unh_marine_navigation#67.\n\n## Goal 2 — Carry-forwards from #205\n\n- [ ] **A clean survey-line set** under control (never cleanly delivered through #173/#186/#201/#205).\n- [ ] **Avoider + chart inflation (rolker/unh_marine_navigation#63)** — the #205 swerving was\n      root-caused to the avoider weaving along the pier's 150 m chart-layer inflation gradient.\n      Re-test the AvoidanceController deviation now that the safety gate changed underneath it.\n- [ ] **Sensor/sonar readiness** for student software integration — M3 pings + 1PPS + QINSy\n      export, SBG nav, AML SVS; survey-data recording pipeline captured end-to-end.\n- [ ] **OTH re-test** (#130) — Starlink-only completed survey line at range.\n- [ ] **Offload QINSy data** (carry-over from #205).\n\n## Goal 3 — Verify the pre-existing yaw-accel finding\n\n- [ ] **velocity_smoother yaw accel/decel** — `nav2_params.240.yaml` currently has\n      `max_accel`/`max_decel` z = **3.0 / -3.0**, but the #36 governor intent (and\n      `test_param_compose`) is **0.5 / -0.5**. Confirm on water whether this is a real\n      governor regression (6× intended yaw accel) or a stale test, and fix/triage. (Surfaced\n      during the #43 review; not yet triaged.)\n\n## Success criteria\n\nCA safety gate validated on water (slowdown + reverse-stop behaving, no deadlock, viz +\nsole-publisher confirmed, fallback drilled) with the yaw-passthrough path left off pending\nthe sim test; a clean survey-line set recorded with valid M3/SBG/SVS data; one OTH line.\nLogs at `docs/logs/2026/2026-MM-DD_\u003chost\u003e_logs.md` per the per-deployment convention.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}